---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { briefFields, projectBrief } from '../lib/project-brief';
import { allTechniqueSlugs, techniqueBySlug, taxonomy } from '../lib/content';
const root = new URL(url('/'), Astro.site).toString().replace(/\/$/, '');
const concepts = [
  ...allTechniqueSlugs.map(slug => ({ title: techniqueBySlug(slug)!.title, markdown: root + '/techniques/' + slug + '.md' })),
  ...taxonomy.threads.map(t => ({ title: t.title, markdown: root + '/threads/' + t.id + '.md' })),
];
---
<Base title="Use this site with your AI · Gradient Ascent" description="Describe your project, copy a brief, and ask your own model to recommend fitting concepts and an implementation plan.">
  <div class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow muted">Apply it to your project</div><h1>Describe your task. Let your AI consult the guide.</h1><p>Use your own model to choose an approach that delivers your outcome and the amount of work you want to hand over. Give it a brief, or ask it to fetch the reference directly. You do not need to choose a level first.</p></div>
  <div class="apply-intro">
    <section class="panel"><h2>1. Describe the work</h2><p>Describe what starts the process, what should be ready at the end, and what you want to do yourself. Leave unknowns blank so your model can ask.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h2>2. Hand it to your model</h2><p>Copy or download the brief below and attach relevant workflow files in your own agent. Your model should ask a few short, numbered questions to clarify how much work you want to hand over before recommending a design. If your model can browse, it can fetch the guide and relevant concept pages itself.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h2>3. Review the recommendation</h2><p>Check every recurring manual step against the experience you asked for. The plan should explain alternatives, compromises, and how to test the complete workflow.</p></section>
  </div>
  <p class="panel">Levels describe autonomy, not a ranking of solutions. Prefer simplicity among approaches that meet your needs—not by giving unwanted work back to you. A fixed workflow can be fully automated; an agent can be worthwhile when it removes substantial hands-on effort.</p>
  <section class="section"><h2>Build tools, then use them</h2><p class="apply-explainer">For tasks that need custom processing or connections between systems, ask your model to consider a coding agent that builds or adapts a tool, tests it, runs it, and inspects the result. For example, it might create a project-data collector and a report generator, then use them to prepare a weekly report for review. The resulting tools may later run as ordinary software; you do not necessarily need an agent in every recurring run. Compare reuse, development effort, validation, and execution permissions before choosing.</p><p><a href={url('/techniques/coding-agents/')}>Explore coding agents &rarr;</a> · <a href={url('/techniques/agent-harness/')}>See how a harness bounds their work &rarr;</a></p></section>
  <section class="section" id="brief-builder" data-brief-root={root} data-concepts={JSON.stringify(concepts)}>
    <h2>Make your project brief</h2><p>You do not have to know every answer yet. This brief starts a conversation: your model should probe unclear review points, manual steps, and exceptions, then summarize the intended experience. For example: “Should I prepare complete carousels for review, or would you like to choose the photos first?”</p><p class="brief-help">This builder makes text for you to review. It does not call a model or submit your answers. Copy or download before leaving; your entries are not saved by this site.</p>
    <div class="brief-grid">
      <div class="brief-fields">
        <label for="brief-concept">Concept to consider <span>(optional)</span></label>
        <select id="brief-concept"><option value="">Let my model consider the full guide</option>{concepts.map(c => <option value={c.markdown}>{c.title}</option>)}</select>
        <p class="brief-help">A starting reference, not a commitment to use this concept.</p>
        {briefFields.map(f => <div class="brief-field"><label for={`brief-${f.key}`}>{f.label}</label><p id={`hint-${f.key}`} class="brief-help">{f.hint}</p>{f.key === 'automation' ? <><input id="brief-automation" data-brief-field="automation" list="automation-options" aria-describedby="hint-automation" placeholder="Choose or type your preference" /><datalist id="automation-options"><option value="Help me perform the steps."/><option value="Prepare the result automatically; I review it."/><option value="Complete the process automatically; involve me only for exceptions."/><option value="Help me decide."/></datalist></> : <textarea id={`brief-${f.key}`} data-brief-field={f.key} rows="3" aria-describedby={`hint-${f.key}`}></textarea>}</div>)}
      </div>
      <div class="brief-output"><h3>Your brief to copy or download</h3><p class="brief-help">The preview updates as you type. Your model will make the recommendation in your own conversation.</p><textarea id="brief-preview" aria-label="Generated project brief" readonly rows="24">{projectBrief({}, root)}</textarea><div class="brief-actions"><button class="button" type="button" id="copy-brief" disabled>Copy brief</button><button class="button secondary" type="button" id="download-brief" disabled>Download Markdown</button></div><p id="brief-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p>The interactive builder needs JavaScript. Copy the blank brief above or <a href={url('/project-brief.md')} download>download the template</a>, then fill it in yourself.</p></noscript>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="workflow-files"><h2>Bring examples of your current workflow</h2><p>Send your brief and relevant files to your own agent together. Text, Markdown, photos, spreadsheets, reports, and other files can show details that are hard to describe.</p><ul class="attachment-checklist"><li><strong>Current input:</strong> a representative file the process starts with.</li><li><strong>Current output:</strong> what you produce today, with what you like and what should improve.</li><li><strong>Desired output:</strong> a finished example or annotated mockup, if you have one.</li><li><strong>Exceptions and instructions:</strong> an awkward case, a failed result, or a format the system must follow.</li></ul><p>In the brief, name each file and its role. Attach those files separately in your agent, or give a local agent explicit access to the relevant folder. The brief download contains text only; this website does not upload or package your files. If a format is unsupported, provide an export or preview your model can inspect.</p></section>
  <section class="section" id="reference-access"><h2>Let your model fetch the reference</h2><p>Give your model your task and this address: <a href={url('/agents.md')}>{root}/agents.md</a>. The guide links to the index, concept definitions, relationships, worked examples, and sources. Models with browsing or retrieval tools can follow those links; fetching is not automatic in every chat app.</p><div class="brief-actions"><a href={url('/agents/')}>Read the model guide</a><a href={url('/llms.txt')}>Reference index</a><a href={url('/project-brief.md')} download>Blank brief</a><a href={url('/llms-full.txt')} download>Download reference text</a></div><p class="brief-help">If your model cannot browse, attach the relevant concept Markdown pages or the reference text along with your brief. The full export is large; individual pages may fit better. Ask the model to state what it actually read.</p></section>
</Base>
<script>
  import { projectBrief, type BriefValues, type ConceptReference } from '../lib/project-brief';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-brief-root]')!;
  const concepts: ConceptReference[] = JSON.parse(root.dataset.concepts!);
  const select = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#brief-concept')!;
  const selected = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('concept');
  const match = concepts.find(c => c.markdown.split('/').pop() === selected + '.md');
  if (match) select.value = match.markdown;
  const preview = document.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#brief-preview')!;
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#brief-status')!;
  const update = () => {
    const values: BriefValues = {};
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement>('[data-brief-field]').forEach(el => { values[el.dataset.briefField as keyof BriefValues] = el.value; });
    preview.value = projectBrief(values, root.dataset.briefRoot!, concepts.find(c => c.markdown === select.value));
    status.textContent = '';
  };
  root.addEventListener('input', update);
  select.addEventListener('change', update);
  update();
  const copy = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy-brief')!;
  const download = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#download-brief')!;
  copy.disabled = download.disabled = false;
  copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(preview.value); status.textContent = 'Copied. Paste this into your conversation with your model.'; }
    catch { preview.focus(); preview.select(); status.textContent = 'Automatic copy is unavailable. The brief is selected; copy it manually.'; }
  });
  download.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([preview.value], {type: 'text/markdown;charset=utf-8'}));
    const a = document.createElement('a'); a.href = href; a.download = 'project-brief.md'; a.click();
    setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(href), 1000);
    status.textContent = 'Brief downloaded. Attach it to your conversation with your model.';
  });
</script>
<style>
  .attachment-checklist { list-style:disc; padding-left:24px; margin:18px 0 }
  .attachment-checklist li { margin:8px 0 }
  h2 { font-size:28px; line-height:1.3; letter-spacing:-.6px; margin-bottom:16px }
  h3 { font-size:22px; line-height:1.35; letter-spacing:-.4px; margin-bottom:12px }
  .apply-intro { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:20px; margin-bottom:32px }
  .apply-intro h2 { font-size:22px; margin-bottom:12px }
  .apply-explainer { max-width:100ch; margin:18px 0 }
  .brief-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:36px; margin-top:24px; align-items:start }
  .brief-output { position:sticky; top:140px; min-width:0 }
  .brief-field { margin-top:22px }
  label { display:block; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:8px }
  .brief-help, label span { color:var(--muted); font-size:14px; margin:8px 0 14px }
  textarea, select, input { width:100%; padding:12px 14px; background:var(--panel); color:var(--text); border:1px solid var(--line-control); border-radius:8px; font:inherit }
  textarea { resize:vertical }
  #brief-preview { font-size:13px; line-height:1.65; min-height:300px; max-height:52vh }
  .brief-actions { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:16px; margin:18px 0 }
  a { color:var(--accent) }
  .secondary { background:var(--panel2); color:var(--text); border:1px solid var(--line-control) }
  #brief-status { min-height:28px; font-size:14px }
  @media(max-width:900px) { .apply-intro,.brief-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr } .brief-output { position:static } }
</style>
